From 8926899ca5c49d0fa3373aae3b3b8d7fedcbacfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:58:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Part C: like-for-like NEMO vs DustPy (point IC, physical-N0
 mapping)

Fixes the DustPy comparison so both codes solve the same discrete problem
(scripts/figures only, no Fortran change):

- A2: compare_dustpy.nemo_curves runs NEMO from the SAME point-sampled IC DustPy
  uses (_run_nemo(..., ic="point")), and uses the physical N0 (N0*m0 for additive)
  for the time mapping, not the grid sums out["N0"]/out["M1"]. Previously NEMO was
  given the bin-integrated IC while DustPy got the point-sampled one, and NEMO's bin
  averages were scored against the exact SAMPLED at m_k -- a bin-average-vs-point
  mismatch that showed a spurious ~5.6% NEMO "error" (really 0.09%/0.35% when scored
  consistently). Physical-N0 mapping is consistent with Part B.
- A3: run_dustpy_coag docstring corrected -- the IC is the exponential sampled at the
  grid masses (dN/dm|_{m_k} * h_k), NOT coag_analytic.exp_ic_bins; states NEMO is given
  the same point IC in the comparison.
- A4: regenerated compare_{constant,additive}.tsv (now include t=0.01) and the figures
  coag_dustpy_l1.* and coag_nemo_vs_dustpy.*. plot_compare_dustpy renders headless
  (Agg) and writes png+pdf; the overlay legend uses T (constant) / tau (additive).

Results (relative L1 on normalised N m^2, 20-bin fiducial grid):
  t=0.01 : NEMO and DustPy agree with the exact and each other to <1% (both codes'
           discretisations coincide at negligible coagulation).
  constant T=0.5/1/2 : NEMO 0.046/0.074/0.087 ; DustPy 0.060/0.110/0.165
  additive  t=0.5/1/2 : NEMO 0.110/0.205/0.370 ; DustPy 0.194/0.311/0.548
  NEMO is closer to the exact than DustPy at every evolved time; both over-diffuse the
  large-mass tail as expected of the k=0 scheme. The residual NEMO-DustPy gap (up to
  ~7% constant, ~22% additive, same IC, same scheme) is reported, not explained; it
  likely reflects DustPy's time integration (untested).

Outlier note (not chased, per brief): additive ratio 1.15 at a_min=5e-8 (149 bins,
outside the fiducial setup) returns cont_L1=1.83. It DID reach its target time; the
cause is a mass-conservation failure -- total dust mass grows to x2.37 of initial by
tau=1 on that extended small-mass grid. The fiducial grid (a_min=5e-7) conserves mass
to 1.0000. Real NEMO behaviour on the extended grid, not a harness artifact; flagged
for a separate look.

